  <running_head>DISSERT. HISTOR. POLIT.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">1146. Eo anno Conradus secundus Im-</l>
    <l n="2">perator ingentes copias pugnatorum</l>
    <l n="3">contra Sarracenos parat : sed pugnat in-</l>
    <l n="4">feliciter.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Ludovicus Rex Galliæ contra infideles</l>
    <l n="6">maximam vim militum cogit.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Rogerius <i>hic cognomine</i> Burfa, <i>teste</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Tyrio lib.xi.cap.xxi. factus est Siciliæ Rex</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>A. cIↄ c xxx. Cinnamus eum perpetuo</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>vocat</i> Σιχτλᾶν Τύραννον<i>: quoniam Grae-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>ci Imperatores ejus infula imperium sibi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>vendicabant. Per Saracenos Africanos in-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>tellige Tunetanos, qui tamen peculiares</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Reges tum nondum habebant, sed parebant</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Almoravidis &amp; Almohadis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16" para="true">1147. Ex Flandria, Anglia, Lotha-</l>
    <l n="17">ringia instructis ducentis navibus bellum</l>
    <l n="18">contra Sarracenos institutum est.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Hoc anno Conradus Imperator trans-</l>
    <l n="20">misso feliciter Bosphoro, prope hostes ac-</l>
    <l n="21">cessit: verum deficiente commeatu, &amp;</l>
    <l n="22">(ut nonnulli ajunt) frumento gypso cor-</l>
    <l n="23">rupto, coactus est continere cursum, &amp;</l>
    <l n="24">copias reducere. Quo cognito, Sarraceni</l>
    <l n="25">à tergo insequentes, aliquot hominum</l>
    <l n="26">millia trucidaverunt.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">Eodem anno confluit ad Imperatorem</l>
    <l n="28">Rex Franciæ : adjuvandi illum studio:</l>
    <l n="29">sed exercitu fame confecto, nihil præcla-</l>
    <l n="30">ri actum est.</l>
    <l n="31" type="foot" para="true">Q 7</l>
    <l n="32" para="true">Eodem</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The Greek words "Σιχτλᾶν Τύραννον" are as printed (Cinnamus' epithet, likely Σικελᾶν Τύραννον; printed form kept). The catchword "Eodem" appears at the foot right. The signature "Q 7" at the foot left is a gathering mark.</notes>
